  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_7' aria-label=\" Dr. Bais Surgical and Medical Institute Pvt. Ltd & Ors. versus Dhananjay Pande pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('7','2026','2026_5_347_363','2026INSC447'); ><font size='4'> <strong>DR. BAIS SURGICAL AND MEDICAL INSTITUTE PVT. LTD & ORS.<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>DHANANJAY PANDE </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 5 S.C.R. 347</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 447</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010001492026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : PAMIDIGHANTAM SRI NARASIMHA</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Whether, in the absence of a formal entry of the respondent no.1&rsquo;s name in the register of members, he could nonetheless be regarded as a &ldquo;member&rdquo; of the appellant-company so as to invoke the jurisdiction of the Company Law Board u/ss.397 and 398 Act, 1956. Headnotes&dagger; Companies Act, 1956 &ndash; ss.2(27), 41, 397, 398, 399 &ndash; &ldquo;member&rdquo; &ndash; High Court and the Company Law Board upheld respondent no.1 as a deemed member of the company, entitled to maintain a petition u/ss.397 and 398 &ndash; Whether the<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 04-05-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 8973/2010</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Dismissed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('7','2026','2026_5_347_363','2026INSC447','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_spl